# A beam at 15 degrees leaves the window half way along. What is left at the end was reflected: everything without an absorber, some if the absorber is too weak (the wall behind it) or too strong (its own front).
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy.
title Tilted beam meeting the edge, absorber strength 0.03
grid dx=0.05 dz=0.25
window width=40 length=150
absorber width=5 strength=0.03
launch gaussian x=0 radius=5 tilt=15
plane end z=150
expect total end 0.339907081 2e-7
expect centroid end 0.6054151 2e-6
expect radius end 11.2690940 2e-6
expect neff 1.417948075 2e-8
